# Root CLAUDE.md is intentionally untracked here (matches canonical policy,
# 2026-07-27 migration) -- content is deliberately local-only. See AGENT.md.
/CLAUDE.md
/GEMINI.md

# Multi-agent session locks (ephemeral — not committed)
.agent/engines/*/session.lock
.agent/locks/

# Gemini CLI project-config symlink (per-machine, ephemeral)
.antigravitycli/

# Build artifacts — not committed
build/
target/

# vendor-sel4-tools build artifacts
vendor-sel4-tools/elfloader-tool/build/

# Tauri v2 generated ACL schemas — regenerated by tauri-build on every build
# (capabilities/ IS committed — it is hand-authored source)
app-workplace-*/src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Generated outputs — not committed
outputs/

# BIM confidential reference content — real home is business-admin/project-floorplates/
preview/

# Local input/library/deployment data — not committed
inputs/
woodfine-bim-library/
woodfine-fleet-deployment/

# Legacy .claude directory (should be .agent symlink — to be fixed)
.claude/

# Sub-clones — managed separately via their own git repos
pointsav-monorepo/
pointsav-design-system/
pointsav-fleet-deployment/
woodfine-fleet-deployment/
pointsav-media-assets/
woodfine-media-assets/

# Local service data + deployment dirs — not committed
logs/
state-corporate/
state-documentation/
state-projects/
state-test/
service-email-egress-ews/
service-email-egress-imap/
woodfine-fleet-deployment/

# OS metadata
.DS_Store
~$*

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Log files — pipeline output; never committed
*.log

# Pipeline analysis output — local only
*-conflict-report.json

# Safety-net archive of misplaced repo clones (cannot be committed; deletion review 2026-07-01)
archive-2026-06-01/

# [Option-A-mailbox-fix] removed 2026-08-27 (Command, at provisioning time) — the
# risk it describes ("cross-archive contamination during git rebase" via
# sovereign_sync.sh) belongs to the retired sovereign_sync.sh architecture
# (deleted per CLAUDE.md §4; every archive is now bootstrapped onto an
# independent per-archive .git repo on cluster/<name> branches). This exact
# block was already found and removed from project-marketing/-system/-console
# 2026-08-25, but apparently never reached canonical main — caught here again
# on a fresh clone rather than reintroducing the bug a 4th time. NEXT.md is
# legitimately real per-repo content and should stay tracked too.

# service-slm/router-trainer — local runtime artifacts (provisioned per-operator,
# not tracked in Git). Kept here so the Python workflow can still find them on
# the filesystem. See cleanup-log.md 2026-04-23 entry for rationale.
service-slm/router-trainer/engine/llamafile
service-slm/router-trainer/**/*.log

# discovery-queue — runtime TX identity data (operator decision 2026-05-16)
# Future disposition: move to service-fs/data/ — tracked as open item
discovery-queue/

# Private key material -- never committed (2026-07-18 security incident:
# operator_private.key, vault_identity.key, and keys/gcp_node_mba_ed25519
# were exposed on public GitHub for 3+ months; history purged via
# git filter-repo). Public keys (*.pub) remain trackable.
system-gateway-mba/operator_private.key
system-gateway-mba/vault_identity.key
system-gateway-mba/keys/gcp_node_mba_ed25519
*.key

# A blanket `.agent/` rule here (copied in from the canonical-mirror repo's own
# .gitignore, correct for vendor/pointsav-monorepo which never carries real
# per-archive .agent/ state, but wrong for a working archive-root repo like this
# one) would silently untrack this archive's entire real .agent/ state — same
# known-bug-patterns.md #2 class already found and fixed in project-marketing,
# project-system, and project-console 2026-08-17/25. Removed before it ever took
# effect here (caught at provisioning, 2026-08-27) rather than repeating the
# incident a 4th time. Only ephemeral session locks stay ignored, per the narrow
# mailbox-file-only block above.
